{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-276993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $15$ and the common ratio is $6?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=15$ and $r=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{15(1-{6}^{N})}{1-6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{5}(1-{6}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({6}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-276993" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276993" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3(6^N-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $3$ and the common ratio is $15?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=15.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{15}^{N})}{1-15} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{14}(1-{15}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{15}{2}(1-{3}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{2}({3}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{16}(1-{15}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{16}({15}^{N}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-5259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $5$ and the common ratio is $2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5(1-{2}^{N})"] ["math" "5({2}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}(1-{2}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}({2}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{10}^{N}-5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5({2}^{N}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $8$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-276476" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276476" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4(3^N-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=-3$ and $r=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =-4[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}] \\\\  & =4[{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}-1] \\\\  & =4({4}^{-N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({4}^{-N}-1)"] ["math" "3({3}^{-N}-1)"] ["math" "4({4}^{-N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}({4}^{-N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}({3}^{-N}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4({4}^{-N}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $5+10+20+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-276481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276481" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5(2^N-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $6+18+54+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=3.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({3}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-276482" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276482" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3(3^N-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-270557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $7+42+252+\\,⋯?$ Express your answer as a function of $N.$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-270557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{7} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=7$ and $r=6.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{1-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(1-{6}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}({6}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-270557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-270557" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-270557" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $2+6+18+⋯?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=2$ and $r=3.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & ={3}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-{3}^{N}"] ["math" "2({3}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}(1-{3}^{N})"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}({3}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{3}^{N}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{3}^{N}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $4+8+16+\\,⋯?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-4(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(1-{4}^{N})"] ["math" "2({2}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "2({4}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "4(1-{2}^{N})"] ["math" "4({2}^{N}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-110180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4({2}^{N}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $324$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 324 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 324 & =27{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=12$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-6(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =6({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-276485" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-276485" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6(3^N-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-277872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $7$th term is $512$ and the common ratio is $2?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-277872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 512 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {2}^{(7-1)} \\\\ 512 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=2.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-8(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =8({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-277872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-277872" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-277872" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8(2^N-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $4$ and the common ratio is $2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 4 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {2}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 4 & =4{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=1$ and $r=2.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{1(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & ={2}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(1-{4}^{N})"] ["math" "4(1-{2}^{N})"] ["math" "4({2}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{2}^{N}-1"] ["math" "{4}^{N}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-67090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{2}^{N}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $5$th term is $2\\,500$ and the common ratio is $5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 2\\,500 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{(5-1)} \\\\ 2\\,500 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ 2\\,500 & =625{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=5.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(-4)}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =-(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & ={5}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "4({5}^{N}-3)"] ["math" "{5}^{N}-1"] ["math" "{5}^{N}-3"] ["math" "{5}^{N}-4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{5}^{N}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $250$ and the common ratio is $5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{3} \\\\ 250 & =125{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{250}{125} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=2$ and $r=5.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(-4)}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8f91728a598edf1a05598c4197c39385b762eac9849eeddc3b1dda230d5765c1"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "4({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}({5}^{N}-1)"] ["math" "{5}^{N}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "q-73423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67c8dd926dfe3f773c842709c4ef26e8d739770b185df99236d95f537d6927e"} {"question" "e-4190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4190.json" "file_sha256" "f224768cceb4f922e406097ea7e72c7e398d79b20d2c831bb81ff45ae98932e0"} {"question" "e-4190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N =\\dfrac{a_1(1-r^N)}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1= -3$ and $r = 2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-1)}(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =3(1-{2}^{N}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4190.json" "file_sha256" "f224768cceb4f922e406097ea7e72c7e398d79b20d2c831bb81ff45ae98932e0"} {"question" "e-4191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of the geometric series $2+8+32+\\cdots \\: ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4191.json" "file_sha256" "e5fc556796b8e5a7ece9d4771cbf8f2a895515ca6e8993d0258c5bde52802c50"} {"question" "e-4191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for $S_N$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4191.json" "file_sha256" "e5fc556796b8e5a7ece9d4771cbf8f2a895515ca6e8993d0258c5bde52802c50"} {"question" "e-4192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $18$ and the common ratio is $3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4192.json" "file_sha256" "3a3973ac7c29d50e943bb7c89b3e2b38c9849ea545b8e3071bd461428b5bd043"} {"question" "e-4192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine $a_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 18 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 18 & =9{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}\t.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for $S_N$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & ={3}^{N}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043929/example-4192.json" "file_sha256" "3a3973ac7c29d50e943bb7c89b3e2b38c9849ea545b8e3071bd461428b5bd043"}] "usage" {"e-4192" [] "e-4190" [] "e-4191" []} "basis" 1731 "retractions" [[17592186082913 :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $2$?"] [17592186082913 :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N =\\dfrac{a_1(1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1= -3$ and $r = 2$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (-3(1 - 2^{N}))/(1 - 2) \\\\\n&= ((-3))/((-1))(1 - 2^{N}) \\\\\n&= 3(1 - 2^{N})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186082914 :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of the geometric series $2+8+32+\\cdots \\:$?"] [17592186082914 :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= \\frac{a_{2}}{a_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{2} \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=4$. Substituting these values into the formula for $S_N$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (a_{1}(1 - r^{N}))/(1 - r) \\\\\n&= (2(1 - 4^{N}))/(1 - 4) \\\\\n&= (2(1 - 4^{N}))/((-3)) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}(1 - 4^{N}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(4^{N} - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186082915 :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $18$ and the common ratio is $3$?"] [17592186082915 :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine $a_1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1}r^{n - 1} \\\\\n18 &= a_{1} \\cdot 3^{(3 - 1)} \\\\\n18 &= 9a_{1} \\\\\na_{1} &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N)}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=3$. Substituting our values into the formula for $S_N$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= (2(1 - 3^{N}))/(1 - 3) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{2}(1 - 3^{N}) \\\\\n&= 3^{N} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
